From 7368ccd75adf801fd44483a2c0bc84cc81ce4721 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:17:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Preserve bounded structured Desktop error details

Problem: plain object throws became fallback in both readableError and
Desktop logging, rendering Prompt failed twice and dropping useful detail.
Why: each boundary only accepted Error/string. Recognized RPC/HTTP object
fields had no shared normalization. The earlier be59e3d362 fix handled JSON
inside strings only, not actual objects.
Root (happened): missing safe diagnostic-envelope normalization.
Root (not caught): notification tests exercised string/Error envelopes only.
Recurrence: adjacent JSON-string regression already fixed; historical Nov14
screenshot exception remains undetermined, not attributed to object throws.

Normalize own diagnostic data properties only (detail/data/error/message),
never serialize the thrown object or invoke its accessors/toJSON. Bound the
walk to six levels, 32 objects and 8192 message characters; retain only known
classification codes up to 128 characters. Share extraction with logging,
retain legacy Error stacks/string handling and recovery classifications,
and omit a redundant fallback title. Preserve specialized refusal handling.

Proof: 10 new object tests RED on unchanged notifications; 37 tests GREEN
across diagnostic, store, timer and component suites. Ten exact mutants for
depth, cycles, nodes, text length, code length, allowlist, accessor reads,
empty text, precedence and code recording all killed by assertions.
Desktop tsc --noEmit passed with 3072 MiB heap (default 2 GiB exhausted).
Focused ESLint/Prettier clean. scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks OK.
No live Desktop deployment or historical trigger proof claimed.
